Found by RUNNING the carry path against a stub venue, not by reading:

  D1  funding is booked per 60s tick, not per 8h print: 60 ticks at 1 bps
      on $100 booked $0.60 (one real print is $0.01); three negative
      MINUTES of the predicted rate unwind the book
  D2  PAPER_TRADING=1 does not gate CarryBroker: USE_TESTNET=0 + PAPER=1
      reports SANDBOX (PAPER) and still sends a mainnet order body
  D3  restart while HEDGED opens a second pair (memory-only position,
      reconcile_pair has zero call sites, orphan check skipped on spot)
  D4  a venue that rejects the perp leg drains the book: 8 spot round trips
      in 10 ticks
  D5  carry_backtest prints QUOTABLE: True on daily closes, no impact
  D6  carry_backtest / venue_study reads never reach the data-read ledger
  D7  borrow_apr silently defaults to 0.05 on the live path
  D8  the pair gate is skipped when pair_risk or snapshot is None
  D12 the engine runs the GATED (in-sample) rule; the clean ungated column
      is not what the book would do

Plus nine FakeClient-only assumptions (spot marketUnit, create response
shape, BTC-denominated spot fee, IM/MM is not headroom, qtyStep 0.001 at a
$100 cap, predicted vs settled funding, ...).

Secrets: 56 commits + 3 committed archives scanned; no key material (test
sentinels only). No REVOKE.md — nothing found. Standing rule written down:
any pre-repo Bybit key is burned.

New read-only tool: tools/session_tail.py prints the four invariants from
the tree and exits 1 on any violation (tests first, 10 new).
README: pointer to INVENTORY; stale test count removed; the false "no venue"
